/Title (Technically, the system follows a client-server architecture where the frontend is developed using HTML, CSS, and JavaScript to provide an interactive and user-friendly interface, while the backend is implemented using Python and Flask to handle business logic and request processing. Communication between the frontend and backend is carried out through RESTful API calls, ensuring smooth data exchange and real-time updates. The system uses a structured storage mechanism such as JSON or a database to maintain patient records, doctor details, and appointment data . When a user interacts with the system, the request is captured by the frontend and sent to the backend server. The backend validates the input, processes the required operation, and updates or retrieves data from the storage layer. The processed response is then sent back to the frontend, which dynamically updates the interface to reflect the latest information. This ensures consistency, accuracy, and immediate feedback to the user. Overall, the system demonstrates a modular and efficient design that enhances usability and provides a strong foundation for future improvements such as AI-based diagnosis, real-time consultation, and advanced natural language processing capabilities.)
